+ {"id":"PERF-013","title":"P3 — the selftest gate spends ~85% of its CPU inside full 00->40 node-provision runs that assert one layer: 2.49 s CPU at d5f7fb2, layer-40 work asserted is 0.01 s","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"reasoning":"Perf tick code-factory-perf-2026-11-03-14-51-11. Measured at d5f7fb2 (board 56 rows) with staged measure.sh + attrib.sh in ~/.hermes/cache/scratch/cf-perf-20261103-1451, /usr/bin/time -p, fresh destinations: `bash tests/selftest.sh` = 2.79 / 2.45 / 2.44 s real with user+sys 2.58 / 2.49 / 2.49 s (34 PASS rows, loadavg 4.8-5.0). The prior perf record at b365792 (07:44) was 1.38-1.54 s wall / 1.38-1.44 s CPU with 28 PASS rows, so the gate's CPU nearly doubled when sections 14 (bb99a5c) and 15 (d088bc6) landed — each runs the full 00->40 provision fixture three times. Per-arm attribution at the tip: full `--apply --repo file://` run (layers 00-40) 0.23-0.26 s CPU; `--check --project demo` (layers 00-30) 0.18 s CPU; the layer-40 work those fixtures actually assert (`git clone --depth 1 file://`) 0.01 s CPU; `python3 -c 'import venv'` 0.02 s; `python3 scripts/disk_floor.py --explain` 0.02 s. tests/selftest.sh invokes project-node.sh 13 times (~8 real runs); at ~0.21 s CPU per run that is ~2.1 s of the 2.49 s gate, ~85%. The gate is dominated by paying every layer for fixtures that assert one row.","acceptance_criteria":"1. scripts/project-node.sh accepts `--layers 20,40` (comma list of the check layers: 00,10,20,30,40), runs only the named layers, prints one `SKIP  layer NN` row per skipped check layer and exactly one `SCOPE: layers <list> (fixture mode — not a node certification)` line; an unknown layer or an empty list exits 2 with the usage line and runs no layer.\n2. A scoped run can never certify a node: under `--apply --layers ...` no .node/node.json is written even when every in-scope layer is green (assert the file is absent), and the summary line keeps its existing shape (`NODE: PASS` / `NODE: FAIL (n)`).\n3. Un